used to prevent divide-by-zero error. Data members numclust and maxiter
represent the number of clusters and the maximum number of iterations,
respectively. Data member seed is a positive integer used to initialize the
random number generator, which is used to select k distinct records from the
dataset as initial cluster centers. Data member distance is a shared pointer
pointing to an object of a distance class.
